<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="59d8a482">&lt;p&gt;
    The technology architecture is typically comprised of infrastructure component diagrams, technology location
    diagrams and network diagrams that portray the overarching technology architecture solution.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The technology architecture is an enabler for enterprise architecture work and is developed after agreement on the
    target business, application and data architectures has been reached. It can also provide governance by using the
    governance framework, established business and other information systems architectures.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="114607c6"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="830e0887"></attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="c846c359"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="f168cf4e">&lt;p&gt;
    To realize the application and data architectures by developing the required logical and physical technology
    components for a given IT solution.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="impactOfNotHaving" nodeId="b0419350"></attribute>
<attribute name="reasonsForNotNeeding" nodeId="249ad701"></attribute>
<attribute name="briefOutline" nodeId="f15ee2f4">&lt;p&gt;
    A technology architecture generally contains the following components:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;Hardware components:&lt;/strong&gt; Physical components such as servers, database racks, desktops, laptops, and
    mobile devices that are part of an enterprise infrastructure.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;Software components:&lt;/strong&gt; Application servers, web servers, and databases that are needed to
    operationalize an IT solution.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;Network components:&lt;/strong&gt; Communication protocols (HTTP, FTP), hub, and switches that are needed to
    interconnect various systems in an IT infrastructure.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;Technology integration patterns:&lt;/strong&gt; These are patterns that are used as integration approaches for
    business systems in an IT infrastructure solution. Examples of patterns include distributed computing and
    node-based architecture.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
